{"choices":[{"message":{"content":"{\n  \"chapter_proposals\": [\n    {\n      \"chapter_id\": \"Ch5\",\n      \"title\": \"微生物干预策略的临床转化现状\",\n      \"purpose\": \"系统评估粪菌移植（FMT）、活体生物药（LBPs）、益生菌及饮食干预在实体瘤 ICI 治疗中的临床试验数据，区分初治与难治人群的疗效差异，明确证据等级（I/II 期 vs III 期），并分析供体选择、安全性及标准化挑战。\",\n      \"scope\": \"涵盖人体临床试验（I-III 期），聚焦实体瘤（黑色素瘤、NSCLC、RCC、CRC 等）。包括 FMT（供体来源、给药途径）、定义菌群（如 CBM588、MRx0518）、益生菌及饮食干预。明确排除纯临床前研究（除非用于解释机制背景）及非 ICI 背景的微生物干预。严格区分观察性关联与干预性因果证据，标注试验设计类型（单臂 vs RCT）及人群特征（初治 vs 经治）。\",\n      \"excluded_source_handles\": [\n        \"P0004\",\n        \"P0028\",\n        \"P0037\",\n        \"P0042\",\n        \"P0055\",\n        \"P0063\",\n        \"P0066\",\n        \"P0069\",\n        \"P0075\",\n        \"P0077\",\n        \"P0078\",\n        \"P0090\",\n        \"P0093\",\n        \"P0096\",\n        \"P0102\",\n        \"P0112\",\n        \"P0113\",\n        \"P0116\",\n        \"P0118\",\n        \"P0120\",\n        \"P0128\",\n        \"P0132\",\n        \"P0136\",\n        \"P0139\",\n        \"P0142\",\n        \"P0146\",\n        \"P0150\",\n        \"P0152\",\n        \"P0157\",\n        \"P0159\",\n        \"P0161\",\n        \"P0162\",\n        \"P0163\",\n        \"P0164\",\n        \"P0168\",\n        \"P0171\",\n        \"P0174\",\n        \"P0175\",\n        \"P0191\",\n        \"P0192\",\n        \"P0194\",\n        \"P0208\",\n        \"P0216\",\n        \"P0218\",\n        \"P0229\",\n        \"P0231\",\n        \"P0242\",\n        \"P0250\",\n        \"P0251\",\n        \"P0255\",\n        \"P0257\",\n        \"P0258\",\n        \"P0262\",\n        \"P0263\",\n        \"P0268\",\n        \"P0273\",\n        \"P0274\",\n        \"P0280\",\n        \"P0285\",\n        \"P0287\",\n        \"P0291\",\n        \"P0294\",\n        \"P0296\",\n        \"P0297\",\n        \"P0303\",\n        \"P0305\",\n        \"P0306\",\n        \"P0311\",\n        \"P0316\",\n        \"P0317\",\n        \"P0319\",\n        \"P0320\",\n        \"P0325\",\n        \"P0328\",\n        \"P0333\",\n        \"P0335\",\n        \"P0336\",\n        \"P0341\",\n        \"P0342\",\n        \"P0351\",\n        \"P0355\",\n        \"P0356\",\n        \"P0358\",\n        \"P0359\",\n        \"P0363\",\n        \"P0369\",\n        \"P0377\",\n        \"P0379\",\n        \"P0381\",\n        \"P0386\",\n        \"P0389\",\n        \"P0392\",\n        \"P0397\",\n        \"P0403\",\n        \"P0406\",\n        \"P0408\",\n        \"P0409\",\n        \"P0414\",\n        \"P0430\",\n        \"P0433\",\n        \"P0439\",\n        \"P0442\",\n        \"P0446\",\n        \"P0455\",\n        \"P0458\",\n        \"P0460\",\n        \"P0464\",\n        \"P0466\",\n        \"P0468\",\n        \"P0470\",\n        \"P0471\",\n        \"P0477\",\n        \"P0486\",\n        \"P0487\",\n        \"P0490\",\n        \"P0494\",\n        \"P0497\",\n        \"P0504\",\n        \"P0506\",\n        \"P0507\",\n        \"P0512\",\n        \"P0514\",\n        \"P0515\",\n        \"P0516\",\n        \"P0518\",\n        \"P0521\",\n        \"P0522\",\n        \"P0523\",\n        \"P0532\",\n        \"P0533\",\n        \"P0534\",\n        \"P0536\",\n        \"P0540\",\n        \"P0543\",\n        \"P0544\",\n        \"P0548\",\n        \"P0549\",\n        \"P0550\",\n        \"P0553\",\n        \"P0555\",\n        \"P0556\",\n        \"P0560\",\n        \"P0562\",\n        \"P0567\",\n        \"P0572\",\n        \"P0574\",\n        \"P0584\",\n        \"P0586\"\n      ],\n      \"substantive_threads\": [\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"FMT 在 ICI 难治人群中的疗效异质性：从概念验证到阴性结果\",\n          \"analysis_task\": \"对比早期黑色素瘤研究（Baruch et al., Davar et al.）与近期 MITRIC 试验（P0578）的结果。分析为何部分试验显示 ORR 提升（~30-40%），而 MITRIC 在广泛实体瘤中 ORR 为 0%。探讨患者选择（快速进展 vs 稳定）、供体匹配（单一响应者供体 vs 混合供体）及免疫微环境基线（髓系抑制）对结果的影响。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0577\",\n            \"P0578\",\n            \"P0212\",\n            \"P0261\",\n            \"P0573\"\n          ],\n          \"evidence_level\": \"Phase I/II 单臂试验；观察性关联；无 III 期 RCT 证据。\",\n          \"limitations\": \"样本量小；缺乏对照组；不同试验间 FMT 制备及给药方案异质性大；MITRIC 阴性结果可能受限于入组患者疾病进展速度过快。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"FMT 在初治人群中的增效潜力：Phase 2 数据与机制新解\",\n          \"analysis_task\": \"重点分析 FMT-LUMINate（P0583）与 TACITO（P0593，来自 tool material）试验数据。对比 NSCLC（单药 ICI）与黑色素瘤（双药 ICI）队列的 ORR 差异（80% vs 75%）。讨论 FMT-LUMINate 提出的新机制假说：疗效可能源于基线有害菌清除而非供体菌定植。评估 TACITO 试验中数值改善但统计显著性未报告的情况。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0583\",\n            \"P0197\",\n            \"P0577\",\n            \"P0304\"\n          ],\n          \"evidence_level\": \"Phase 2 单臂试验；Phase 2a RCT（TACITO，主要结局未发表统计显著性）。\",\n          \"limitations\": \"TACITO 统计显著性未报告；FMT-LUMINate 为单臂设计，ORR 对比历史对照存在偏倚风险；机制假说（有害菌清除）需进一步验证。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"活体生物药（LBPs）与益生菌：标准化菌株 vs 复杂菌群\",\n          \"analysis_task\": \"评估定义明确的菌株制剂（如 CBM588, MRx0518, MET4）的临床进展。对比 CBM588 在 RCC 中维持菌群稳定性（P0006, P0143）与 MRx0518 在难治实体瘤中的安全性及免疫激活信号（P0125, P0230, P0244）。讨论单菌株/定义菌群相对于 FMT 在安全性、标准化及监管方面的优势，以及疗效证据等级的不足。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0006\",\n            \"P0143\",\n            \"P0125\",\n            \"P0230\",\n            \"P0244\",\n            \"P0122\",\n            \"P0178\",\n            \"P0387\"\n          ],\n          \"evidence_level\": \"Phase I/II 试验；临床前数据支持机制。\",\n          \"limitations\": \"多数试验主要终点为安全性或微生物组变化，而非 OS/PFS；疗效信号多为探索性；菌株特异性效应显著，不可泛化至所有益生菌。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"干预相关安全性与毒性：供体特征与治疗背景的情境依赖\",\n          \"analysis_task\": \"分析 FMT-LUMINate 中观察到的严重 irAEs（特别是黑色素瘤双药队列的心肌炎，15% 发生率）与供体菌群（Prevotella 富集）的关联（P0583, P0197）。对比单药 ICI 背景下未观察到类似毒性的情况。讨论 FMT 及 LBPs 的通用安全性风险（如菌血症、irAEs 加重），并明确毒性管理在干预策略中的重要性。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0583\",\n            \"P0197\",\n            \"P0212\",\n            \"P0261\",\n            \"P0567\"\n          ],\n          \"evidence_level\": \"Phase 2 试验安全性数据；观察性关联。\",\n          \"limitations\": \"毒性机制（如 Prevotella 诱导心肌炎）尚未解析分子通路；样本量小导致发生率估计不精确；仅特定 ICI 组合背景下观察到。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"theme\": \"证据等级总结与转化瓶颈：缺乏 III 期 RCT 及标准化\",\n          \"analysis_task\": \"明确陈述目前无已完成并发表主要结局数据的 Phase III RCT。总结 I/II 期试验的共性局限（样本量、异质性、缺乏外部验证）。讨论供体筛选标准、FMT 制备工艺、给药途径及宿主基线微生物组对疗效的影响。指出未来研究需解决标准化及人群分层问题。\",\n          \"key_sources\": [\n            \"P0215\",\n            \"P0451\",\n            \"P0546\",\n            \"P0573\",\n            \"P0574\",\n            \"P0304\"\n          ],\n          \"evidence_level\": \"综述性评估；基于现有试验数据的推断。\",\n          \"limitations\": \"无 III 期数据支持常规临床应用；标准化方案尚未确立；供体 - 受体匹配策略未明。\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"transition_logic\": \"本章结尾将总结微生物干预目前仍处于探索阶段，疗效受人群及方案影响显著，且存在特定安全性风险。这将自然过渡到 Ch6（微生物组与免疫治疗毒性的关联），深入探讨毒性发生的微生物机制及预测标志物；同时为 Ch7（方法学挑战与未来研究方向）中关于标准化及 III 期试验设计的需求提供实证依据。\",\n      \"supplement_requests\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"是否有已完成的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在 ICI 治疗实体瘤中的疗效？\",\n          \"reason\": \"确认证据等级上限，避免过度宣称临床转化成熟度。\",\n          \"current_knowledge\": \"现有数据主要为 I/II 期试验（FMT-LUMINate, MITRIC, MIMic, TACITO）。TACITO 为 Phase 2a RCT，数值改善但统计显著性未报告。无已完成并发表主要结局数据的 Phase III RCT。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验中 FMT 联合 ICI 的 ORR 数据是多少？供体菌群特征（如 Prevotella）与毒性（心肌炎）的关联机制是什么？\",\n          \"reason\": \"获取关键疗效及安全性数据，用于对比不同人群及方案的风险收益比。\",\n          \"current_knowledge\": \"NSCLC 队列 ORR 80%，黑色素瘤队列 ORR 75%。Prevotella 富集供体在双 ICI 背景下与心肌炎风险增加相关（15% 发生率），单药背景下未观察到。具体分子机制未解析。\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"MITRIC 试验中 FMT 在 ICI 耐药患者中的 ORR 及 PFS 数据是多少？为何结果为阴性？\",\n          \"reason\": \"平衡阳性结果，客观呈现干预策略在难治人群中的局限性。\",\n          \"current_knowledge\": \"ORR 0%，中位 PFS 1.5 个月。阴性原因可能包括患者疾病进展过快、供体匹配不佳及免疫微环境限制（髓系偏倚）。\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"directed_reads\": [\n        \"P0583\",\n        \"P0578\",\n        \"P0577\",\n        \"P0125\",\n        \"P0006\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"screened_sources\": []\n}","reasoning_content":"The user wants a chapter proposal for Chapter 5 of a review on the gut microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) in solid tumors.\nThe chapter title is \"微生物干预策略的临床转化现状\" (Current Status of Clinical Translation of Microbiome Intervention Strategies).\nThe purpose is to summarize clinical trial results of interventions like FMT and probiotics in overcoming ICI resistance, analyze donor selection, safety, and durability, and clarify evidence levels.\nKey questions involve efficacy/safety of interventions, existence of Phase III RCTs, and differences between treatment-naive vs. refractory populations.\nEvidence notes indicate mostly Phase I/II trials (FMT-LUMINate, MITRIC, MIMic, TACITO), no completed Phase III RCTs with published primary outcomes. Need to highlight evidence levels and population differences.\nI need to use the provided source_routing to select relevant sources for this chapter.\nI need to structure the chapter proposal with substantive threads, scope, boundaries, transitions, and specific source handles.\nI must not write the full chapter, but plan it.\nI must adhere to the constraints: no \"Introduction/Conclusion\" chapters, focus on substantive analysis, distinguish association vs causation, retain source limitations, use Chinese for text, keep English for paper titles/specific terms if needed.\nI need to check the shared_level1_outline to ensure alignment with the overall review structure.\nI need to check the chapter_tool_materials for specific data points (e.g., ORR values for specific trials) to ensure accuracy in the planning.\n\nPlan for Chapter 5:\n1.  **Scope**: Focus on interventional studies (FMT, probiotics, defined consortia, diet) in solid tumors receiving ICIs. Distinguish between treatment-naive (first-line) and ICI-refractory (second-line+) populations.\n2.  **Substantive Threads**:\n    *   **FMT in ICI-Refractory Populations**: Analyze the mixed results (positive signals in melanoma vs. negative in MITRIC). Discuss donor selection (responder vs. healthy) and mechanisms (clearance of harmful bacteria vs. engraftment).\n    *   **FMT in Treatment-Naive Populations**: Discuss recent Phase 2 data (FMT-LUMINate, TACITO) showing higher ORR/PFS. Highlight the shift from \"overcoming resistance\" to \"enhancing first-line efficacy\".\n    *   **Probiotics and Defined Consortia**: Evaluate specific strains (e.g., CBM588, MRx0518) vs. commercial probiotics. Discuss the \"one-size-fits-all\" vs. personalized approach.\n    *   **Safety and Toxicity**: Analyze irAEs, specifically the link between donor microbiome (e.g., Prevotella) and severe toxicity in combination ICI settings (FMT-LUMINate findings).\n    *   **Evidence Level & Future Directions**: Explicitly state the lack of Phase III RCTs. Discuss standardization challenges (donor screening, preparation, delivery).\n3.  **Sources**: Select from the routed sources that specifically discuss clinical trials, FMT, probiotics, and intervention strategies.\n    *   Key Trial Reports: P0577 (MIMic), P0578 (MITRIC), P0583 (FMT-LUMINate), P0593 (TACITO - from tool material), P0125 (MRx0518), P0230 (MRx0518 safety), P0006/P0143 (CBM588).\n    *   Reviews on Interventions: P0178, P0212, P0215, P0261, P0387, P0451, P0546, P0567, P0573.\n    *   Mechanism/Safety: P0197 (FMT-LUMINate abstract), P0212 (Meta-analysis), P0304 (Systematic review).\n4.  **Limitations**: Emphasize that most data are Phase I/II, small sample sizes, heterogeneity in protocols, and lack of Phase III confirmation. Distinguish between association (microbiome changes) and causation (clinical benefit).\n5.  **Transitions**: Connect to Ch6 (Toxicity) regarding safety signals, and Ch7 (Future Directions) regarding the need for Phase III trials and standardization.\n\nLet's refine the source selection based on the provided routing list.\nRelevant sources for Ch5:\n- P0577 (MIMic trial)\n- P0578 (MITRIC trial)\n- P0583 (FMT-LUMINate trial)\n- P0125 (MRx0518 Phase I/II)\n- P0230 (MRx0518 safety)\n- P0006/P0143 (CBM588 in RCC)\n- P0178 (Clinical evidence for FMT, LBPs, consortia)\n- P0212 (Meta-analysis on FMT)\n- P0215 (Microbiome Modulation review)\n- P0261 (Facts and Hopes)\n- P0387 (Immunotherapy with guts)\n- P0451 (Systematic Review)\n- P0546 (Gut microbiome in modulating ICIs)\n- P0567 (Harnessing the gut microbiome)\n- P0573 (Optimizing FMT)\n- P0304 (Systematic review on FMT/antibiotics)\n- P0291 (Role of intestinal microbiome)\n- P0355 (Clinical Evidence review)\n- P0357 (Probiotic use review)\n- P0470 (Meta-analysis)\n- P0543 (Leveraging gut microbiota)\n- P0544 (Modulating in CRC)\n- P0555 (Unveiling interplay)\n- P0572 (Therapeutic interventions)\n- P0574 (Gut dysbiosis)\n- P0584 (Navigating gut-metabolite-immune)\n- P0586 (Engineered bacteria - though AML focus, relevant for LBP discussion)\n- P0190 (OMVs - relevant for non-live interventions)\n- P0307 (Yeast delivery - relevant for novel vectors)\n- P0473 (MaaT034)\n- P0552 (MaaT034 abstract)\n- P0122 (MET4)\n- P0244 (MRx0518 neoadjuvant)\n- P0249 (Black Raspberry diet)\n- P0156 (Dietary interventions)\n- P0252 (Diet and Probiotics)\n- P0321 (GI tumors microbiome group)\n- P0324 (GI resistance mini review)\n- P0343 (Integrative Oncology)\n- P0445 (Affordable immunotherapy)\n- P0482 (bEVs)\n- P0486 (Metabolites in CRC)\n- P0490 (Enhancing immunotherapy)\n- P0494 (Multi-modal bacteria)\n- P0497 (Hidden army)\n- P0504 (Urothelial carcinoma)\n- P0505 (Levofloxacin + CBM588)\n- P0506 (Combination strategies)\n- P0507 (Metabolites reshaping TIME)\n- P0512 (Moving on from Metchnikoff)\n- P0514 (CRC review)\n- P0515 (Metabolites review)\n- P0516 (GI cancers review)\n- P0518 (PD-1/PD-L1 metabolites)\n- P0521 (Gut-tumor connection)\n- P0522 (Impact of microbiome)\n- P0523 (Gut-targeted strategies)\n- P0532 (Focus on gut microbes)\n- P0533 (Tumor-Associated Microbiome)\n- P0534 (Secondary Qualitative Review)\n- P0536 (Chinese review)\n- P0540 (Mechanisms and therapeutic potential)\n- P0548 (Effect on systemic immunity)\n- P0549 (HCC therapy)\n- P0550 (Ayurvedic interventions)\n- P0553 (Metabolites in CRC)\n- P0556 (Immune checkpoint therapy dilemmas)\n- P0560 (Gut Microbiota and Tumor Immune Escape)\n- P0562 (RCC resistance)\n- P0577 (MIMic)\n- P0578 (MITRIC)\n- P0583 (FMT-LUMINate)\n- P0584 (Navigating gut-metabolite-immune)\n- P0586 (Engineered bacteria)\n\nI will select the most pertinent ones for the proposal to avoid overcrowding, focusing on those with specific trial data or high-quality reviews on interventions.\nKey Trial Sources: P0577, P0578, P0583, P0125, P0230, P0006, P0143.\nKey Review Sources for Intervention Landscape: P0178, P0212, P0261, P0387, P0451, P0546, P0567, P0573.\nKey Safety/Toxicity Sources: P0197, P0212, P0583.\nKey Mechanism/Strategy Sources: P0178, P0473, P0552, P0482.\n\nI need to make sure I don't duplicate content with Ch6 (Toxicity). Ch5 should focus on efficacy and safety as a constraint for intervention, while Ch6 focuses on the microbiome-toxicity association broadly. I will limit toxicity discussion in Ch5 to intervention-specific safety signals (e.g., FMT-related irAEs).\n\nI will structure the proposal with:\n- Chapter ID, Title, Purpose, Scope.\n- Substantive Threads (ordered themes).\n- Source Handles (relevant for this chapter).\n- Excluded Source Handles (if any routed sources are truly out of scope for *this* chapter, though most intervention-related ones should be included).\n- Supplement Requests (if any data is missing, e.g., specific Phase III trial IDs).\n- Directed Reads (if any specific papers need deep reading for this chapter).\n- Transition Logic (to Ch6 and Ch7).\n\nI must ensure I don't claim Phase III evidence exists. I must highlight the MITRIC negative result vs FMT-LUMINate positive result contrast.\nI must distinguish between FMT, Probiotics, and Defined Consortia.\nI must mention the donor selection issue (Responder vs Healthy).\nI must mention the safety signal (Prevotella/Myocarditis in FMT-LUMINate).\n\nLet's draft the JSON.","role":"assistant"},"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"logprobs":null}],"object":"chat.completion","usage":{"prompt_tokens":62319,"completion_tokens":6033,"total_tokens":68352,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2534,"text_tokens":6033},"prompt_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":62319}},"created":1791137998,"system_fingerprint":null,"model":"qwen3.5-plus","id":"chatcmpl-0d1ccb58-d1d1-91c4-affc-403eb5ea579f"}